en: {
  nav1:'What it is', nav2:'Examples', nav3:'Get started',
  badge:'v1 beta · OBS 28+ · Twitch · Claude skill',
  h1:'OBS overlays designed for <em>your channel</em>, not a template with your name on it',
  lead:'Paste your Twitch channel. Claude looks at what you play, how you talk to your chat and what makes your stream yours, then hands you a complete overlay pack ready for OBS. No code.',
  ctaStart:'Start now →', ctaDl:'Download the skill',
  you:'You:', chatQ:'Make me an overlay pack. My channel is twitch.tv/your_channel',
  chatA:'I looked at your last streams: mostly Elden Ring, no-hit runs, Spanish-speaking chat, you count deaths by hand in the title…<br>Here are two directions. Which one feels like you?',
  getEy:'What you get', getT:'A complete pack, not loose pieces', getL:'You pick a direction, Claude builds the pack, and you get a zip with everything ready for OBS.',
  c1t:'Scenes', c1p:'Starting soon, Be right back, Ending, plus your main scenes: game, just chatting, coding…',
  c2t:'Alerts', c2p:'Sub, resub, gifted sub, sub bomb, raid and bits, written in your channel’s language and humour.',
  c3t:'Chat & goals', c3p:'On-screen chat, sub goal and camera frame that match the rest of the pack.',
  c4t:'Pieces made for your format', c4p:'Death counter, boss tracker, topic agenda, day counter… whatever your stream actually needs.',
  c5t:'Control panel inside OBS', c5p:'Buttons, hotkeys and chat commands for your mods to drive every piece live.',
  c6t:'One-click install in OBS', c6p:'Creates scenes and sources for you, already positioned. Running it again is safe: it repairs without duplicating.',
  exEy:'Not templates', exT:'One sub, five different channels', exL:'Every pack starts from the idea behind your channel, not from a style menu.',
  g1:'<b>Corner shop</b> · the alert prints like a till receipt', g2:'<b>Game show</b> · marquee lights, confetti and a prize',
  g3:'<b>Metro line</b> · each stream topic is a station', g4:'<b>Pilgrimage</b> · tar seeps through the stone',
  g5:'<b>No-hit run</b> · a thin banner that stays out of the fight', g6:'<b>Control panel</b> · press F9 or a mod types a command',
  stEy:'Start now', stT:'Up and running in 3 minutes', stL:'Install the skill, ask Claude for your pack and connect it to OBS.',
  req2:'✅ Claude account with <i>Code execution</i> turned on', req3:'✅ Twitch channel',
  tab1:'Claude app (web / desktop)', tab3:'As a plugin',
  a1t:'Download the skill', a1p:'Get <code>overlay-generator.zip</code> from the '+REL+'latest release</a>. <strong>Don’t unzip it.</strong>',
  a2t:'Turn on code execution', a2p:'In Claude: <strong>Settings → Capabilities</strong> and turn on <i>Code execution and file creation</i>.',
  a3t:'Upload the skill', a3p:'<strong>Customize → Skills</strong>, click <strong>+</strong> → <i>Create skill → Upload a skill</i>, pick the zip and make sure it’s switched on.',
  aNote:'On Team and Enterprise plans, an owner may need to allow skills first.',
  k1t:'If it’s already in your account', k1p:'Skills enabled in your Claude account sync to Claude Code automatically. Check with <code>/skills</code>.',
  k2t:'Or install it locally', k2p:'Unzip it into your skills folder:',
  p1t:'Install it straight from the repository', p1p:'Inside Claude Code, run:',
  copy:'Copy', copied:'Copied!',
  useEy:'How to use the skill', useT:'Ask Claude for your pack', useL:'Start a new chat and say something like:',
  pr1s:'With your channel', pr1:'“Make me an OBS overlay pack. My channel is twitch.tv/your_channel”',
  pr2s:'Without a channel', pr2:'“I stream Minecraft hardcore in French, chill vibe. I want a day counter and a goal for 10 subs.”',
  f1:'<b>You</b>paste your channel or describe your stream', f2:'<b>Screenshots</b>1–2 of your stream (optional, but helps a lot)',
  f3:'<b>Questions</b>camera or VTuber, goals, sponsors, topics to avoid', f4:'<b>2 directions</b>pick one or ask for changes', f5:'<b>Your pack</b>zip + preview.html + guide',
  tip:'💡 Before touching OBS, double-click <code>preview.html</code> to see the whole pack.',
  obsEy:'Set up OBS', obsT:'About 5 minutes, and only once', obsL:'The pack uses OBS’s own WebSocket. Nothing else to install: no Python, no server, no account.',
  o1t:'Unzip the pack in a permanent folder', o1p:'For example <code>C:\\Overlays\\my-pack</code>.',
  o2t:'Turn on the WebSocket', o2p:'<i>Tools → WebSocket Server Settings</i>, tick <i>Enable</i>, keep authentication on and copy the password with <i>Show Connect Info</i>.',
  o3t:'Add the panel as a dock', o3p:'<i>Docks → Custom Browser Docks…</i>, give it a name and paste the path of <code>panel.html</code> as URL, e.g. <code>file:///C:/Overlays/my-pack/panel.html</code>.',
  o4t:'Connect and install', o4p:'Paste the password into the panel, click <strong>Connect</strong> then <strong>⚙ Install in OBS</strong>. Scenes and sources are created for you.',
  o5t:'Optional: hotkeys', o5p:'<i>Settings → Hotkeys</i>, search for the <code>OVG ·</code> entries and set a key on <i>Show</i>. Works with Stream Deck too.',
  o6t:'Optional: chat commands', o6p:'Type your channel in the panel and click <i>Listen to chat</i>. Your mods can use <code>!death</code>, <code>!next</code>…',
  o7t:'Go live!', o7p:'Keep the panel open while you stream: it’s the brain of the pack. You can minimise it, but don’t close it.',
  obsWarn:'⚠️ Don’t unzip the pack in Downloads or in a OneDrive/Dropbox synced folder: if the folder moves, the overlays break.',
  updT:'🔄 Update your pack', updP:'Send Claude your zip (or just <code>pack.json</code>) and say what you want: “add a boss tracker”, “louder alerts”. Unzip the new one over the old one and, if there are new pieces, click <i>Install in OBS</i> again. Your counters are kept.',
  faqT:'Frequently asked questions',
  q1:'The overlay is blank or doesn’t react', a1:'<li>Check that the panel says <i>Connected to OBS</i>.</li><li>If you added a source by hand, untick “Local file” and paste the full <code>file:///…</code> address.</li><li>Right-click the source → Refresh.</li>',
  q2:'“Panel closed” appears on stream', a2:'The panel dock was closed. Open it again from <i>Docks</i> and the notice disappears within seconds.',
  q3:'A hotkey doesn’t work inside a game', a3:'Some games in exclusive fullscreen or with strict anti-cheat swallow key presses. Use “Borderless window”, the chat command or a Stream Deck.',
  q4:'Does it support follows, donations or channel points?', a4:'Not yet. The pack reads chat anonymously (subs, resubs, gifts, raids, bits). For the rest, the guide shows how to keep those alerts in StreamElements or Streamlabs, styled to match.',
  q5:'Does it work with YouTube or Kick?', a5:'Scenes, panel and pieces work anywhere OBS does. Alerts and chat are Twitch-only in v1; YouTube and Kick are on the roadmap.',
  q6:'What about my privacy?', a6:'No accounts, no servers, no tracking. Everything runs in your OBS, on your computer.',
  finT:'Your channel deserves more than a template', finL:'Download the skill and have your pack ready before your next stream.',
  finDl:'Download overlay-generator.zip', finBug:'Report a bug',
  foot:'Made by '+GH+' with Claude. Not affiliated with OBS Project, Twitch or Anthropic.'
},
